This commit documents the automated conflict resolution performed by claude
for upstream commit 028363685bd0b7a19b4a820f82dd905b1dc83999.

claude's resolution process:
================================================================================
Build succeeded (rc=0) on both arm64 and x86 with only pre-existing/unrelated warnings (dtsi PCI reg warning and a modpost.c toolchain warning — neither touches the changed files). No new warnings from this commit.

**Conflict resolution summary:**

The upstream commit removed the `encap_sk` caching mechanism from `esp_find_tcp_sk()`/`esp6_find_tcp_sk()`. The conflict arose because at the point where upstream declared `struct net *net = xs_net(x);` (to later use `net->ipv4.tcp_death_row.hashinfo`), this 5.15 branch instead calls `inet_lookup_established(xs_net(x), &tcp_hashinfo, ...)` inline with the global `tcp_hashinfo` (the per-netns hashinfo refactor hadn't landed yet on this branch). So there was no local `net` variable to preserve, and the `esk` declaration from the old caching code (removed by this patch) also collided at the same spot.

Resolution: dropped both the `esk` declaration (part of the removed caching logic) and the `net` declaration (unneeded here since this branch already calls `xs_net(x)` inline at the lookup site), keeping the rest of the patch — including the two added `sock_put(sk)` calls and the `include/net/xfrm.h`/`net/xfrm/xfrm_state.c` hunks — exactly as upstream. This is a pure conflict-context resolution; no logic beyond what the original commit intended was changed.

Committed as `c25aea18b6a03` with `(cherry picked from commit 028363685bd0b7a19b4a820f82dd905b1dc83999)`, author preserved as Sabrina Dubroca, commit message unchanged.
